# Custom tooltips (no native `title` for definitions)

Dotted-underline jargon and definitions must use the same **`.node-tooltip`** chrome as map bubbles — not the browser’s default `title` tooltip.

## Marking copy

- Use **`applyDefinitionTooltipAttrs`** from `@/lib/canvas-sdk/useDefinitionTooltips` (or equivalent markup):
  - Class: **`ifai-term`**
  - **`data-ifai-tooltip-title`** — term label (usually the visible word)
  - **`data-ifai-tooltip-desc`** — plain-language definition
  - **`tabIndex={0}`** and **`aria-label`** for keyboard/accessibility
- **Do not** set **`title`** on definition marks. Native tooltips fight the custom cursor and look inconsistent.

## Runtime

- **`useDefinitionTooltips`** (wired in `CanvasShell`) shows/hides the shared tooltip on hover and focus for `[data-ifai-tooltip-desc]`.
- Panel glossary injection lives in **`annotateGlossary`** (`panel-interactions.ts`).

## Other `title` usage

- **`title` on icon-only controls** (zoom, close, theme toggle) is OK for supplementary hints when there is no dotted underline.
- If you add a **new** dotted-underline + definition pattern anywhere (sidebar HTML, modals, React components), use the data attributes above — never `title` alone.

## Visual

- Style terms with **`.ifai-term`** (`border-bottom: 1px dotted` in `canvas-sdk.css`).
- Definition tooltips use **`.node-tooltip-definition`** (fixed position, high z-index for modals).
